preConditionHook:
// Brooks's shaved top / shaved bottom: the close is within shaveOffsetPoints
// of the bar's high (long) / of its low (short), so there is no tail at the
// far end.
//
// consecutiveBars (AMENDMENT, Grimes G01-09): EVERY one of the last
// consecutiveBars bars must pass that test, not merely this one. Grimes reads
// a RUN of closes on the absolute extreme as short-term exhaustion rather than
// strength, so his natural placement is NEGATED, as a block on a fresh
// with-trend entry; his own reading is three bars, and his words are "close on
// their absolute highs", i.e. offset 0, so the default 0.25 is the loose
// reading. THE DEFAULT IS 1, at which the loop runs exactly once over bar 0
// and the rule is the single-bar test it has always been -- el_gt is the exact
// complement of el_le under the EL relational tolerance, so every existing
// placement is unchanged bar for bar. The MicroChannelRunLength / minTicks
// precedent: a run length lands as an input on the single-bar rule rather than
// as a near-duplicate file.
//
// The source states the tolerance in TICKS. `minmove` and `pricescale` are
// UNKNOWN in EL_FEATURES and ctx exposes no tick size at all, so the tolerance
// is carried as a PRICE-POINT input, per AUTHORING.md and the convention the
// rest of this batch follows (CloseNearPriorLow, LimitEntryAtMicroGapEdge).
// The default 0.25 is the book's one tick at the Emini's tick size and is
// therefore instrument-specific -- a grid-pass concern.
//
// Not CloseRangePosition, which puts the close in the upper FRACTION of the
// bar's own range: an absolute offset is far stricter on a wide bar and far
// looser on a one-tick bar, so the two fire on different bars. Not
// ConsecutiveUpBars, which tests the close against the bar's own open.
//
// All-of-N written the way ShrinkingBodies writes it -- start true and let any
// failing bar clear the flag -- so the loop runs unconditionally and
// EasyLanguage's lack of short-circuiting cannot matter. Both sides are
// computed here rather than in the conditions for the same reason.
//
// The flags are class members and persist across bars; both are reset at the
// top of the hook rather than relied on to start true.
//
// Deepest bar touched: consecutiveBars - 1.
shavedTop = true;
shavedBottom = true;
for (kk = 0; kk < (int)consecutiveBars; ++kk) {
    if (el_gt(high[kk] - close[kk], shaveOffsetPoints)) shavedTop = false;
    if (el_gt(close[kk] - low[kk], shaveOffsetPoints)) shavedBottom = false;
}
